WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.558 --> 00:00:04.058
(upbeat electronic music)

00:00:04.997 --> 00:00:06.758
- [Announcer] Baseball
in Korea, is like nothing

00:00:06.758 --> 00:00:08.255
you've ever seen.

00:00:08.255 --> 00:00:11.407
And its fans, they're in
a league of their own.

00:00:11.407 --> 00:00:14.438
- [Announcer] The atmosphere
at a game, it's cathartic,

00:00:14.438 --> 00:00:15.271
it's cleansing.

00:00:15.271 --> 00:00:17.805
No one cares what you look
like or how badly you sing

00:00:17.805 --> 00:00:20.508
or dance, as long as you're
cheering for Lotte Giants,

00:00:20.508 --> 00:00:23.287
everyone's happy together.

00:00:23.287 --> 00:00:27.454
(crowd chanting in foreign language)

00:00:30.394 --> 00:00:33.038
- [Announcer] Baseball was
first brought to Korea in 1905

00:00:33.038 --> 00:00:35.715
by American missionaries,
and the people of South Korea

00:00:35.715 --> 00:00:38.361
loved it; it became one of the country's

00:00:38.361 --> 00:00:40.825
most popular sports, and in 1982,

00:00:40.825 --> 00:00:43.218
Korea made its love of the game official

00:00:43.218 --> 00:00:45.514
and formed the Korean
Baseball Organization,

00:00:45.514 --> 00:00:47.616
or KBO for short.

00:00:47.616 --> 00:00:49.423
The league started with six teams.

00:00:49.423 --> 00:00:51.633
Today, there are 10, and the Lotte Giants

00:00:51.633 --> 00:00:53.052
from the city of Busan are one

00:00:53.052 --> 00:00:55.985
of two inaugural franchises left.

00:00:55.985 --> 00:00:57.896
Their fans are legendary.

00:00:57.896 --> 00:00:58.729
(crowd cheering)

00:00:58.729 --> 00:01:00.365
Their cheermaster is a celebrity.

00:01:00.365 --> 00:01:02.452
(yelling in foreign language)
(crowd cheering)

00:01:02.452 --> 00:01:03.587
What's a cheermaster?

00:01:03.587 --> 00:01:05.267
Don't worry, we'll get to that.

00:01:05.267 --> 00:01:09.108
First, meet Lotte's
most unlikely superfan.

00:01:09.108 --> 00:01:10.575
- I came to Korea in 2008,

00:01:10.575 --> 00:01:12.588
and I teach at a small university.

00:01:12.588 --> 00:01:15.279
I was living in Ulsan,
and we took a field trip

00:01:15.279 --> 00:01:18.986
to Sajik Stadium, and, uh, it was just amazing.

00:01:18.986 --> 00:01:22.951
Gradually, I've become a Lotte
Giant's superfan, I guess.

00:01:22.951 --> 00:01:24.586
(upbeat music)

00:01:24.586 --> 00:01:25.695
- [Announcer] And, in the nine years

00:01:25.695 --> 00:01:27.961
he's been going to games,
he's become so well known

00:01:27.961 --> 00:01:30.257
in the stands that people regularly stop

00:01:30.257 --> 00:01:32.314
and ask to take photos with him.

00:01:32.314 --> 00:01:34.121
- [Kerry] I really don't
know why I became so famous

00:01:34.121 --> 00:01:37.104
other than it's perhaps because I'm big

00:01:37.104 --> 00:01:38.601
and I look like Santa Claus,

00:01:38.601 --> 00:01:41.625
and in a crowd of 20,000 Koreans,

00:01:41.625 --> 00:01:44.654
there are not many guys that look like me.

00:01:44.654 --> 00:01:48.571
(speaking in foreign language)

00:01:54.629 --> 00:01:57.590
- [Announcer] Choi Joon
Suk is a mountain of a man.

00:01:57.590 --> 00:02:00.423
He's a first baseman,
your prototypical masher

00:02:00.423 --> 00:02:02.398
in the middle of the batting order.

00:02:02.398 --> 00:02:03.839
He's known for crushing baseballs

00:02:03.839 --> 00:02:05.505
and his epic bat flips.

00:02:05.505 --> 00:02:08.502
Because in the KBO, bat
flips are quite common,

00:02:08.502 --> 00:02:11.134
and no big deal, whereas
in the major leagues

00:02:11.134 --> 00:02:14.771
in the States, it's seen
as a sign of disrespect.

00:02:14.771 --> 00:02:16.958
We'll just let the slugger explain this.

00:02:16.958 --> 00:02:20.875
(speaking in foreign language)

00:02:33.841 --> 00:02:35.788
- [Announcer] OK, fine, not much to say.

00:02:35.788 --> 00:02:37.047
What about you, foreign Major-Leaguer

00:02:37.047 --> 00:02:40.197
and Lotte Giants team captain, Lee Dae Ho?

00:02:40.197 --> 00:02:44.114
(speaking in foreign language)

00:02:52.363 --> 00:02:53.975
- [Announcer] Some say it's nationalistic.

00:02:53.975 --> 00:02:55.752
Some say it's entertaining.

00:02:55.752 --> 00:02:58.007
And some say very little at all.

00:02:58.007 --> 00:03:00.302
(upbeat music)

00:03:00.302 --> 00:03:03.597
Regardless of theory,
one thing is certain.

00:03:03.597 --> 00:03:06.295
Bat flips are absolutely mesmerizing,

00:03:06.295 --> 00:03:08.989
and in the KBO, you
get your money's worth.

00:03:08.989 --> 00:03:11.822
(classical music)

00:03:17.793 --> 00:03:20.204
(announcers speaking in foreign language)

00:03:20.204 --> 00:03:22.787
(upbeat music)

00:03:23.646 --> 00:03:25.397
- I tell everyone that, to me,

00:03:25.397 --> 00:03:27.006
the MLB is like an opera,

00:03:27.006 --> 00:03:30.172
and the Lotte Giants at
Sajik is like rock and roll.

00:03:30.172 --> 00:03:32.839
(upbeat music)

00:03:35.548 --> 00:03:38.359
The atmosphere, the energy.

00:03:38.359 --> 00:03:41.161
And I only planned to go to a few games,

00:03:41.161 --> 00:03:43.770
and for the last three years,
I've had season tickets

00:03:43.770 --> 00:03:47.145
at Sajik, so I'd probably
been to about 120 games

00:03:47.145 --> 00:03:49.885
every year for the last three years.

00:03:49.885 --> 00:03:50.909
(chanting in foreign language)

00:03:50.909 --> 00:03:53.305
I get asked a lot: Why
do I go to so many games?

00:03:53.305 --> 00:03:55.377
And, in one word, it's fun.

00:03:55.377 --> 00:03:59.074
I'm, 63 years old, and I don't
think I should apologize

00:03:59.074 --> 00:04:01.748
for wanting to have fun.

00:04:01.748 --> 00:04:04.214
- [Announcer] Rambunctious
crowds, electric atmosphere,

00:04:04.214 --> 00:04:07.518
and bat flips are all part
of the KBO experience.

00:04:07.518 --> 00:04:10.933
But what really sets the KBO
apart is the cheermaster.

00:04:10.933 --> 00:04:13.407
And, Lotte's is top dog.

00:04:13.407 --> 00:04:15.143
So, what does a cheermaster do?

00:04:15.143 --> 00:04:17.203
(screaming in foreign language)

00:04:17.203 --> 00:04:20.453
(loud, thumping music)

00:04:23.446 --> 00:04:27.363
(speaking in foreign language)

00:04:56.897 --> 00:04:59.147
(chanting)

00:05:00.455 --> 00:05:03.758
- Cho Ji-Hoon is so famous
because of his skill,

00:05:03.758 --> 00:05:05.577
because of his passion.

00:05:05.577 --> 00:05:08.784
He is working almost 100% of the game.

00:05:08.784 --> 00:05:11.849
He's talking, he's singing, he's dancing.

00:05:11.849 --> 00:05:14.048
He is the heart of the Lotte Giants.

00:05:14.048 --> 00:05:16.680
(upbeat electronic music)

00:05:16.680 --> 00:05:20.597
(speaking in foreign language)

00:05:32.264 --> 00:05:36.771
(chanting in foreign language)

00:05:36.771 --> 00:05:40.771
(speaking in foreign language)

00:05:52.213 --> 00:05:55.909
(singing in foreign language)

00:05:55.909 --> 00:05:59.826
(speaking in foreign language)

00:06:04.029 --> 00:06:05.877
- [Announcer] The Lotte Giants are Busan's

00:06:05.877 --> 00:06:07.456
only professional sport's team.

00:06:07.456 --> 00:06:09.685
The entire city rallies behind them.

00:06:09.685 --> 00:06:12.567
They are a raucous and
rambunctious fan base,

00:06:12.567 --> 00:06:16.739
they make sure you feel, or
rather, hear their presence.

00:06:16.739 --> 00:06:18.989
(cheering)

00:06:20.519 --> 00:06:24.436
(speaking in foreign language)

00:06:59.578 --> 00:07:01.485
- I'm probably the luckiest man in Korea,

00:07:01.485 --> 00:07:03.079
because I've made so many friends,

00:07:03.079 --> 00:07:06.200
and had so many unique
and special experiences

00:07:06.200 --> 00:07:07.908
all because of baseball.

00:07:07.908 --> 00:07:09.941
Many of my Korean friends
speak very little English,

00:07:09.941 --> 00:07:11.662
I speak very little Korean,

00:07:11.662 --> 00:07:13.480
But, we have a common language.

00:07:13.480 --> 00:07:15.541
And that language is the Lotte Giants.

00:07:15.541 --> 00:07:18.208
(upbeat music)

